From: Asgard
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-combo: do not disable pipe_clk twice when USB init times out

pipe_clk is enabled in qmp_combo_com_init() and disabled in qmp_combo_com_exit(). qmp_combo_usb_power_on()
never enables it, but its timeout path still disabled it, and qmp_combo_usb_init() then called com_exit(),
which disabled it again ("gcc_usb3_prim_phy_pipe_clk already disabled"). On the AYN Thor one PHY init
timeout on a USB-C cable wake (2026-10-12 09:55) left the clock refcount one short, the PHY ran without a
pipe clock from then on, and every later resume failed the same way (dwc3_qcom_pm_resume returns -110), with
the controller holding its 1 GB/s DDR vote through sleep until a reboot.
---
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -3909,16 +3909,12 @@
 	ret = readl_poll_timeout(status, val, !(val & PHYSTATUS), 200,
 			PHY_INIT_COMPLETE_TIMEOUT);
 	if (ret) {
+		/* pipe_clk is com_init()'s: the caller's com_exit() disables it, not us */
 		dev_err(qmp->dev, "phy initialization timed-out\n");
-		goto err_disable_pipe_clk;
+		return ret;
 	}
 
 	return 0;
-
-err_disable_pipe_clk:
-	clk_disable_unprepare(qmp->pipe_clk);
-
-	return ret;
 }
 
 static int qmp_combo_usb_power_off(struct phy *phy)
